   "text": "I read the molecule as a thalidomide-type cereblon ligand joined through a linker to a pyrimidine kinase-binding group. I worked through it region by region.\n\n**Left end (glutarimide and isoindoline-dione).**\n- The 2,6-dioxopiperidin-3-yl ring is attached through its C3 to the isoindoline-1,3-dione nitrogen.\n- The benzo ring of the isoindoline carries an O\u2013CH2\u2013C(=O)\u2013NH group at the 4-position.\n- The glutarimide C3 is drawn with plain bonds, so I gave it no stereo.\n\n**Linker.** I counted the zigzag between the amide NH and the piperidine nitrogen as 7 CH2 groups.\n\n**Piperidine.** It is N-substituted by the heptyl chain. Its C3 carries an NH drawn on a wedge bond.\n- At C3, the neighbours are C4 (drawn up), C2 (the CH2 next to the ring N, lower left) and the wedged NH (lower right).\n- The priorities are N > C2 > C4 > H, and the H points away from the viewer.\n- Going N \u2192 C2 \u2192 C4 runs clockwise on the page, so the centre is R.\n- In the SMILES I write this centre as `[C@H]`, which I checked by permutation to correspond to R.\n\n**Right end.** The NH on piperidine C3 attaches to C2 of a pyrimidine. That pyrimidine has Cl at C5 and an NH-aryl group at C4. The aryl group is a phenyl bearing an ortho isopropylsulfonyl group, S(=O)(=O)CH(CH3)2.\n\nSMILES: O=C1CCC(N2C(=O)c3cccc(OCC(=O)NCCCCCCCN4CCC[C@H](C4)Nc4ncc(Cl)c(Nc5ccccc5S(=O)(=O)C(C)C)n4)c3C2=O)C(=O)N1"
